  <model metaid="meta_losartan_intestine" id="losartan_intestine" name="Model for losartan absorption in the small intestine" substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <h1>Model for losartan absorption</h1>
        <ul>
          <li>dissolution of the tablet and transit into the gut lumen</li>
          <li>absorption of losartan (<code>LOSABS</code>, OATP2B1) into the enterocytes, efflux
back into the lumen (<code>LOSEFL</code>, P-glycoprotein/ABCB1) and transport into
the portal blood (<code>LOSEX</code>); the absorption is nearly complete, the
bioavailability of 33 % is the hepatic first pass [Lo1995]</li>
          <li>the fecal excretion of the content of the gut lumen with the transit
through the colon (<code>METEXC_k</code>): unabsorbed losartan and the E3174 and
other metabolites of the bile</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The species of the gut lumen (<code>*_lumen</code>) are concentrations in the lumen
volume <code>Vlumen</code>.</p>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
